# How to cite Cinoc — Citation File Format 1.2.0 (https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
#
# TO BE COMPLETED BY THE MAINTAINER: the repository declares no author name,
# so only the alias of the repository's public owner is written below. Add
# each author's `given-names`, `family-names` and `orcid` (and `affiliation`).
#
# Deliberately absent until the `v1.0.0` tag exists (S32, S35): `version`,
# `date-released` and `doi`. The package version is computed from the git tag
# (setuptools_scm); a `version` written here before that tag would contradict
# it, and tests/guardrails/test_citation.py refuses one that no tag carries.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Cinoc, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: Cinoc
abstract: >-
  Cinoc is a deterministic, reproducible benchmark for transcription
  pipelines (OCR, HTR, vision-language models, OCR followed by an LLM) on
  heritage documents. It runs competing pipelines over a corpus and its
  ground truth, and writes a self-contained HTML report of metrics and
  significance tests; no language model writes the report, every number is
  an auditable function of the inputs.
authors:
  - alias: maribakulj
repository-code: "https://github.com/maribakulj/cinoc"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - ocr
  - htr
  - vlm
  - llm
  - transcription
  - benchmark
  - evaluation
  - cer
  - wer
  - alto
  - page-xml
  - iiif
  - post-correction
  - cultural-heritage
  - digital-humanities
